  "notes": "USAGE:\nCasual slang for making a mistake, usually a big or embarrassing one, with a sense of \"I really did it this time\". The past form やらかした is common as an exclamation on realizing a mistake. It can also mean doing something outrageous: ⟦あいつ→あいつ：08267_aitsu⟧、⟦また→また：00969_mata⟧やらかした.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- しまった: oh no! (the moment of realizing a mistake)\n- ⟦やっ→やる：02980_yaru⟧ちゃった: I've done it now (casual)\n- ヘマ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to make a blunder\n- ⟦しくじる→しくじる：25843_shikujiru⟧: to fail at something one attempted",
